cff-version: "1.2.0"
type: software

title: "adaptive-playbook: Operational Implementation of the Adaptive Interfaces Guide"
date-released: "2026-04-05"

authors:
  - family-names: Case
    given-names: Denise M.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6165-7389"
    affiliation: "Northwest Missouri State University, USA"

repository-code: "https://github.com/adaptive-interfaces/adaptive-playbook"
url: "https://github.com/adaptive-interfaces/adaptive-playbook"
license: MIT

abstract: |
  An operational playbook for configuring agents to produce team-conforming output.
  Defines a repeatable execution process for establishing priors, loading adaptive
  interface layers (ACS, ATD, AO, domain context), and evaluating results against
  team conventions and domain correctness. Focuses on actionable setup rather than
  conceptual guidance.

keywords:
  - agent engineering
  - agent configuration
  - adaptive interfaces
  - adaptive onboarding
  - adaptive conformance
  - team-conforming output
  - priors
  - domain context
  - AI-assisted development

message: "If using this project, please cite it as described in this file."
